I updated the dump and paranoid patches linked to my Nethack page at
http://www.netsonic.fi/~walker/nethack.html

The newest version of the dump patch now has support for macro %d in the
filename. When the file is written, %d is replaced by the current date
and time in format YYYYMMDDHHMMSS.
So, if the filename is defined like
OPTIONS=dumpfile:/tmp/%n-%d.nh
and your character called Foo dies on the 15th of August 2011 at
16:44:15, the actual filename will be /tmp/Foo-20110815164415.nh.

An incremental diff for the people with the previous version of the patch
can be found at
http://www.netsonic.fi/~walker/nh/dump-date.diff

The paranoid batch had a little bug that may have caused string overflow
when dipping something that has been #named both individually and
non-individually with very long names.

An incremental diff from the previous version can be downloaded at
http://www.netsonic.fi/~walker/nh/paranoid-overflow.diff

I also updated the combined diff that has all my patches in one diff,
but didn't make another incremental diff for that, use the separate
incremental diffs.

